{# IN·08 — the most recent photographs and documents on any incident.

   EVIDENCE BELONGS TO THE INCIDENT, never to a person's upload: a photograph
   filed with a patrol observation travels with it when the observation becomes an
   incident, and keeps its ORIGINAL timestamp and position. So each tile names the
   case it belongs to, and opens that case rather than the file — this is a
   dashboard, and what a tile here answers is "where did this turn up".

   THE TILE IS THE STORAGE'S, drawn from the same macro the case file draws, in
   the shape a read-only listing wants: nothing to remove, so the whole cell is
   the link. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiStorage/upload/_tile.html.twig' as evidence %}
{% if not door('case-files.read', area) %}
    {# EVIDENCE IS THE CASE FILE, and the case file is a concern of its own: a
       tile here names the case a photograph belongs to and opens it, which is
       the same fact the record's Evidence card is withheld for. #}
    <div class="c" data-w="evidence">
        <span class="tab">Latest evidence<span class="src">· withheld</span></span>
        <div class="use">What is attached to this area's case files is withheld from you. There is evidence here; it is not yours to read.</div>
    </div>
{% else %}
<div class="c" data-w="evidence">
    <span class="tab">Latest evidence<span class="src">· photographs and documents · newest first</span></span>
    <div class="i-evgrid">
        {% for file in dashboard.evidence %}
            {%- set label = file.ownerLabel ~ ' · ' ~ file.name -%}
            {{ evidence.kept({
                name: file.name,
                label: label,
                thumbState: file.thumbState.value,
                thumbUrl: file.hasThumbnail ? path('storage_evidence_show', {key: file.thumbKey}) : '',
                detailUrl: file.ownerUrl,
                title: 'none' == file.thumbState.value ? '' : label,
            }) }}
        {% else %}
            <div class="use">No evidence attached in this window.</div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="use">Evidence belongs to the incident, never to a person's upload — a photo filed with a patrol observation travels with it when the observation becomes an incident, and keeps its original timestamp and position.</div>
</div>
{% endif %}
